      <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">
        The Tang Suit: China''s Festive Jacket
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Despite its name, the Tang suit (tangzhuang) isn''t from the Tang dynasty — it''s a modern evolution of Qing-era Magua riding jackets, popularized globally when world leaders wore them at the 2001 APEC summit. Today, it''s China''s go-to festive menswear, and Beijing''s hutong tailors are the best place to get one made.
      </p>

